FFmpeg master 969c7eb09198 (2026-08-31), not in release/9.0 after 9.0.2;
CVE-2026-107678:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/969c7eb091989a664cb7bf66a1f02051cc46cb52

libavutil: av_encryption_init_info_free() freed the list of init infos
recursively, one stack frame per entry; the mov demuxer makes an entry of every
pssh box, so an mp4 with tens of thousands of small pssh boxes exhausted the
stack: ffmpeg and ffprobe crash. Now a loop. The quadratic time of such a file
(master 71403a21cd03 and d1434518, which add a function to libavutil) is not
taken: a few seconds of CPU, bounded by the size of the upload.

--- a/libavutil/encryption_info.c
+++ b/libavutil/encryption_info.c
@@ -218,16 +218,19 @@ AVEncryptionInitInfo *av_encryption_init_info_alloc(
 
 void av_encryption_init_info_free(AVEncryptionInitInfo *info)
 {
-    uint32_t i;
-    if (info) {
+    while (info) {
+        AVEncryptionInitInfo *next = info->next;
+        uint32_t i;
+
         for (i = 0; i < info->num_key_ids; i++) {
             av_free(info->key_ids[i]);
         }
-        av_encryption_init_info_free(info->next);
         av_free(info->system_id);
         av_free(info->key_ids);
         av_free(info->data);
         av_free(info);
+
+        info = next;
     }
 }
 
